cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its data, please cite the paper."
title: "The Cost of Saying Hello: An Empirical Study of Handshake Overhead in AI Agent Communication Protocols"
authors:
  - family-names: Varshney
    given-names: Pranav
    affiliation: University of Michigan
    email: pvarsh@umich.edu
abstract: >-
  A phase-decomposed benchmark of the connection-establishment handshake in
  three AI agent communication protocols (MCP, A2A, ACP), measuring round
  trips, per-phase latency, wire bytes, capability-metadata context cost,
  and failure behavior with the protocols' official SDKs.
keywords:
  - agent communication protocols
  - Model Context Protocol
  - A2A
  - handshake overhead
  - connection establishment
  - benchmarking
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pvarshh/handshake-benchmark"
